# Licensing

This is a multi-licensed repository. There is no single repository-wide
software license. A file's license is determined by the explicit mapping in
[`REUSE.toml`](REUSE.toml), with attribution and provenance recorded in the
owning extension's README and in [`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).

- Repository scaffolding, validation tooling, and `apple-wloc` use the MIT
  License. This covers the local `apple-wloc` manifest and documentation, not
  its remote scripts. Those scripts are fetched from `Yu9191/wloc` commit
  `ea204aedfd36b3d407c3506ac25db506a6c1b419`, whose tree carries the standard
  AGPL-3.0 text and whose README separately requires authorization for
  commercial-product or application-store use. The selected candidate records
  non-commercial use. This repository distributes none of the script bytes,
  and [`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) records the boundary.
  The complete project MIT text is in
  [`LICENSES/MIT.txt`](LICENSES/MIT.txt); retained upstream MIT notices are in
  [`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
- `bilibili-cleaner` uses `GPL-3.0-only`, matching the `kokoryh/Sparkle` module
  it accompanies. It does not vendor the four generated JavaScript bundles;
  the gateway fetches those pinned scripts at runtime. It distributes adapted
  source from two upstream jq programs inside `extension.yaml`; the local forms
  add type guards and remain GPL-3.0-only preferred source. The complete GPL
  text is in [`LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt`](LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt).
- `weatherkit` and `youtube-cleaner` use `Apache-2.0`, matching the upstreams
  whose published bundles they load. Neither vendors upstream source. The
  complete Apache text is in
  [`LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`](LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).
- `testflight-region-unlock` and the separately authorized `zhihu-cleaner`
  port are Kelee-derived adapted material under `CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0`. The
  complete text is in
  [`LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt`](LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt).

One extension's license never overrides another extension's license. A
repository-level license found in a mirror also does not override a more
specific license supplied by the original author of a mirrored file. See
[`KELEEONE-LICENSE.md`](KELEEONE-LICENSE.md) for the deliberately narrow scope
of the KeleeOne license boundary.
